[ext_resource type="Material" path="res://resources/tiles/road.tres" id="2_road"]

; A banked quarter turn to the right, 63 m radius - the catalog's CornerRadius.
;
; Three points rather than two so the middle one can carry tilt, which is the bank. The ends are at
; zero tilt because the chain has nowhere to record a roll: a piece that leaves banked hands its
; neighbour a frame that says nothing about the bank, and the neighbour is built flat against it.
;
; 0.5 rad is about 29 degrees. The hand-built corners used a 60 degree lip solved against
; v = sqrt(g * r * tan(theta)) so that riding the wall flat out was the car holding itself up - if
; you want that back, raise this and check it against TopSpeed. Flip the sign if it banks the wrong
; way: the outside of a right-hand turn is the left.
[sub_resource type="Curve3D" id="Curve_right"]
